    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0319" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg247"/>

                <head>No. 15.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to Mr. West.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 12,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my dispatch to Mr.
                    Drummond of the 9th July last, I transmit herewith for your information, copies
                    of a further correspondence I have had with the legation of the United States,
                    in this country, relative to the arrest of Mr. Joseph B. Walsh, who has been
                    imprisoned at Kilmainham under the protection of person and property act in
                    Ireland, 1881, and has now been released by direction of the lord-lieutenant of
                    Ireland, on the ground of the ill-health of the prisoner.<anchor n="*"
                        xml:id="d140-f1"/></p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
